 1370 f8bc:             ;
 1371 f8bc:             ; the CRTC registers R0..R15 for vinit, as measured on the card 2026-10-21: an 11.0592 MHz crystal (Q2, SV4 on 1-2),
 1372 f8bc:             ; 6 dots a character (IC28 a 74163), 8 scan lines a row (RA0..2): a 1.8432 MHz character clock, 117 characters a line
 1373 f8bc:             ; = 63.5 us (15.75 kHz), 32 rows + 6 lines = 262 lines (60.1 Hz), non-interlaced - a TV-rate monitor. 80 columns
 1374 f8bc:             ; (43.4 us of text) fit such a monitor's visible ~48 us with a margin each side (R2 94 centres them); a 9 MHz crystal
 1375 f8bc:             ; gave room for only 64. The character EPROM gets ~540 ns a character (an MBM2732A is a 450 ns part). R1/R6 follow
 1376 f8bc:             ; VROWS; tools/vidsim.py timing checks a table.
 1377 f8bc:             ; 2026-10-22: R0..R3 per card (vmode picks one, R6), R4..R15 common. A V1.3 card runs from 12 MHz: 6 dots a 2.0 MHz
 1378 f8bc:             ; character, 127 a line (15.75 kHz), 80 x 24 (40 us of text, R2 98 centres it); 8 dots a 1.5 MHz character, 95 a line
 1379 f8bc:             ; (15.79 kHz), 64 x 24 - the 64-column table proven on the monitor 2026-10-21 (then from 9 MHz / 6, the same 1.5 MHz).
 1380 f8bc:             ; 2026-11-10 (branch video-v2): the V2.0 card, 12 MHz like the V1.3; the V1.0-V1.2 table (11.0592 MHz: 116, 80, 94, 9)
 1381 f8bc:             ; is gone with the card.
 1382 f8bc: 7e 50 62 0a vcr80:  DB 126,80,98,10   ; DOTS open: 6 dots, 80 x 24 (R0 total-1, R1 displayed, R2 sync position, R3 sync width)
 1383 f8c0: 5e 40 4b 08 vcr64:  DB 94,64,75,8     ; DOTS fitted: 8 dots, 64 x 24
 1384 f8c4: 1f          vcrtab: DB 31             ; R4  vertical total - 1 (rows)
 1385 f8c5: 06                  DB 6              ; R5  vertical total adjust (scan lines)
 1386 f8c6: 18                  DB VROWS          ; R6  rows displayed
 1387 f8c7: 1b                  DB 27             ; R7  vertical sync position (row)
 1388 f8c8: 00                  DB 0              ; R8  interlace mode: off
 1389 f8c9: 07                  DB 7              ; R9  scan lines per row - 1
 1390 f8ca: 67                  DB 067h           ; R10 cursor start line 7, blinking (1/16 field rate)
 1391 f8cb: 07                  DB 7              ; R11 cursor end line 7
 1392 f8cc: 00                  DB 0              ; R12 start address high
 1393 f8cd: 00                  DB 0              ; R13 start address low
 1394 f8ce: 00                  DB 0              ; R14 cursor address high
 1395 f8cf: 00                  DB 0              ; R15 cursor address low
